<technical>
- TypeScript/React for Remotion v4.x
- 15 FPS (or as specified)
- Frame-perfect: duration_seconds * FPS
- Assets: staticFile() relative to public/
- Use interpolation and spring APIs
- Only installed libraries
</technical>

<quality>
Visual: Smooth animations, readable text, clear hierarchy, consistent colors, balanced layout.
Narrative: Clear segment structure, supportive transitions, matching pacing, visual emphasis, engaging arc.
Technical: Perfect audio sync, background music at 20-30% volume, seamless looping/fades, frame-accurate timing, proper error handling, correct duration sums.
Code: Lightweight, focused, minimal files, efficient rendering.
</quality>

<performance_optimization>
- Use JPEG format unless transparency required (PNG is slower)
- Target 1080p/720p resolution and ≤30fps unless specified
- Increase `<OffthreadVideo>` cache size for better memory utilization
- Prefer `renderMedia()` over sequential `renderFrames()` calls
- Use MP3 audio codec instead of AAC for faster encoding
- Avoid GPU-heavy CSS: minimize box-shadow, gradients, blur filters
- Prefer transform/opacity animations (GPU-accelerated efficiently)
</performance_optimization>

<workflow>
1. Read Remotion skills
2. Parse outline XML
3. Verify assets in public/
4. Calculate frame timings
5. Plan file structure (minimize files)
6. Create/modify root composition
7. Create segment components
8. Integrate assets
9. Add transitions
10. Polish animations
11. Verify syntax and paths
</workflow>

<best_practices>
- Read skills first
- Modular components for common patterns
- Performance: useMemo, useCallback
- Declarative animations
- staticFile() for assets
- TypeScript for type safety
- Lightweight code
- Remotion patterns for rendering
</best_practices>